# Negative-control mutant — the payment-method submit refuses a no-op change (AC-8, R31)
#
# Scenario it must flip: contract.feature > "Nothing is sent when my selection
#   changes nothing" (bdd.md A22(d)). The no-op refusal lives in the ACTION
#   layer, guarding `update` (R31): no `SET_PAYMENT_METHOD` is sent
#   when the open form's model names no method or the method the contract
#   already uses; the call resolves `false`, no request leaves the module.
# Test that goes red: contract.mutations.int.test.ts >
#   "useContract — nothing is sent when my selection changes nothing (AC-8,
#   bdd.md A22(d))" — BOTH rows:
#     "AC-8 sends nothing when I pick no method at all"
#     "AC-8 sends nothing when I pick the stored method my contract already uses"
#   (with the guard gone the PATCH reaches the wire, so
#   `observed.matching(.../payment_details)` is non-empty and each `toEqual([])`
#   flips). Both rows drive `setPaymentMethod`, which opens + sets + submits and
#   so routes through the guarded `update`.
# Mutation: `update` drops its R31 no-op refusal (the model/current
#   comparison never fires), so an empty or unchanged selection is written.
#
# Apply with:  git apply <this file>   (run from repo root)
# Revert with: git apply -R <this file>
diff --git a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract/useContract.actions.ts b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract/useContract.actions.ts
index 80a0623a5..3c8e7db48 100644
--- a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract/useContract.actions.ts
+++ b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract/useContract.actions.ts
@@ -126,7 +126,7 @@ export function createContractActions(
       state,
       "contract.paymentDetailsId"
     );
-    if (!model?.paymentDetailsId || model.paymentDetailsId === current) {
+    if (false) {
       return false;
     }
 
